vidual, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000766"} "Team, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "923618"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350427"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "19020353"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000833"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/742"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Large Hill / 10 km, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 February 2018"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/937"} "Alpensia Cross-Country Centre, Alpensia Resort, Mountain Cluster, Daegwallyeong"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/9000763"} "48 from 16 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Large hill ski jumping (one jump) and 10 kilometres skiing. Pursuit-style cross-country race, with skiers leaving in order of their finish in the ski jumping, so that final placement determined by final placement in cross-country ski race."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The large hill favorites were two Germans, " [:a {:href "/athletes/119468"} "Eric Frenzel"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/119470"} "Johannes Rydzek"] ". Frenzel had won the last five overall World Cup titles, and was the defending gold medalist, while Rydzek had won four gold medals at the 2017 World Championships. Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/110874"} "Akito Watabe"] " was also considered a medal contender."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Watabe took the lead in the ski phase, followed by Norwegian " [:a {:href "/athletes/137749"} "Jarl Magnus Riiber"] ", while the German triumvirate – Frenzel, Rydzek, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/127857"} "Fabian Rießle"] " – were in fourth, fifth, and sixth, respectively, with Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/127371"} "Willi Denifl"] " in third."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The ski phase was won by Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/109591"} "Alessandro Pittin"] ", who had been a non-factor in the jump, and would finish only 27th overall. Rießle had the third-fastest ski time, but Rydzek was fourth in ski time, and held on to win the gold medal in a remarkably close finish. The three Germans came to the line almost together, with Rydzek winning by 0.4 seconds over Rießle, with Frenzel another four-tenths back, as Germany swept the medals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Frenzel had already won gold on the normal hill at PyeongChang and would win another gold in the team event, along with Rydzek and Rießle. Rießle had been the bronze medalist in this event at Sochi, but had finished seventh on the normal hill in PyeongChang, done in by a poor jumping performance."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was the first medal sweep in a Nordic combined individual event since 1936, as Norway had swept all the medals in the only Nordic combined event on the program in 1924, 1928, 1932, and 1936."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time Margin"] [:th {} "Ski Jumping, Large Hill"] [:th {} "Cross Country Skiing, 10 km"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119470"} "Johannes Rydzek"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "23:52.5"] [:td {} "131.2 (5)"] [:td {} "23:52.5 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/127857"} 